  "answer": "This has been reported before. The Quick Access popup always opens in the bottom-right corner, even when the taskbar is on the left or top edge. PowerToys#45712 (v0.97.2) is the same request and asks for either autodetection of the tray position or a setting to pick the corner. PowerToys#23857 is an older report of the same behavior. It was closed as a duplicate of #23772, with a hotfix planned at the time, but the problem is back in current versions. PowerToys#6751 has a comment about the same thing. There is no fix or setting yet. For now, open Quick Access with a global shortcut, or open PowerToys from the tray icon's context menu. Please add a thumbs-up or your details to #45712 so the request gets more weight."
 },
